{
  "_comment": [
    "Announces this module's clinical data to the medreport reporting module.",
    "",
    "This file is the ENTIRE integration. patientview gains no dependency on medreport:",
    "no import, no interface, no library. medreport discovers this manifest on the classpath",
    "of every started module, reads what data exists, and calls the named PatientviewService",
    "methods reflectively. Those methods already return Map<String,Object> / List<Map<...>>,",
    "so the contract between the two modules is JDK types plus this file - nothing more.",
    "",
    "Because the call goes through Context.getService(PatientviewService.class), this module's",
    "own @Authorized advice still runs on every fetch. medreport cannot be used as a way",
    "around patientview's access rules; requiredPrivilege below is an additional filter that",
    "also hides the data from the report's selection tree, so a user who may not view it",
    "cannot even ask for it.",
    "",
    "If medreport is not installed, nothing reads this file and nothing changes."
  ],

  "id": "patientview",
